        // So after 6 moves, the permutation is the identity.
        // This means the state repeats every 6 moves.

        // So we only need to consider n % 6.
        // Let r = n % 6.
        // We know the final position is x.
        // We need to find the initial position p such that after r moves, p becomes x.

